electric Effect - ContentsDa Science Experiment", "keywords": ["experiment", "environment", "piezoelectric", "science", "contentsda"], "long_description": "1. Add potassium tartrate and sodium carbonate to a beaker with water.\n2. turn on the heater until the solution becomes clear.\n3. remove the impurities in the clear solution using filter paper and pour the filtered solution into a container and wait for it to crystallize.\n4. Strike the crystallized piezoelectric element and see if it generates electricity.\n5. Assemble the piezoelectric element onto a piezoelectric plate.\n6. Try tapping the piezoelectric plate with a hammer or hitting it with a ball to turn on the lantern and charge the battery.", "short_description": "Discover how certain materials generate electricity when subjected to mechanical stress. This experiment explores the applications of the piezoelectric effect in generating renewable energy."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/privacy-policy-en/", "developer_terms_of_service_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/terms-and-conditions-en/", "publisher_name": "ContentsDa Inc", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1043107547362485"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "NOT_REQUIRED", "play_area": "MOVEMENT", "recommended_graphics": null, "recommended_memory_gb": null, "recommended_processor": null, "supported_in_app_languages": ["en", "ko"], "supported_input_devices": ["OCULUS_TOUCH"], "supported_player_modes": ["STANDING", "ROOM_SCALE"], "supported_tracking_modes": [], "user_interaction_modes": ["SINGLE_USER"], "id": "8609132155873567"}, "review_messages": []}]}, "cover_square_image": {"uri": "https: